<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">haggle</ansi>

Haggle is a rogue's skill. With a haggler at your side, the market
gives your company better prices: cheaper to buy, dearer to sell.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">The numbers</ansi>

  2% better per level, 8% at level 4, on top of your standing's prices
  (<ansi fg="command">help standing</ansi>). A buying price rounds up, so a cheap good may
  not come down at all. A sale always pays less than the cheapest price
  anyone could buy the good back for, so buying and selling straight back
  never makes money, whoever haggles.

<ansi fg="command">market</ansi> lists the haggled prices and names who haggles; each trade
says how much gold the haggling won. Inns and shops keep their own prices.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Usage:</ansi>

  There is no command: it happens when you trade.
  <ansi fg="command">autoskill haggle off</ansi> trades at the plain prices.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help market</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help specialists</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help standing</ansi>.
